{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDI0L0JlY29taW5nJTIwSGl0Y2hjb2NrJTIwVGhlJTIwTGVnYWN5JTIwT2YlMjBCbGFja21haWwlMjAlMjgyMDI0JTI5Lw","type":"movie","name":"Becoming Hitchcock The Legacy Of Blackmail","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/zPaESWatFlE1URgz1uIJ6aDm2d7.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/nBVloGKjgnUybCPNIeStGNqowb2.jpg","description":"Narrated by historian, critic and filmmaker Elvis Mitchell, this documentary reflects the development of the iconic filmmaker's signature style, through the making of one of his benchmark films, Blackmail. The documentary highlights the birth of the \"Hitchcock Touch\" at a period when talking pictures first emerged and explores his trademark themes, like such as murder, suspense and cool blondes. While focusing on Blackmail, the documentary reveals how this film also foreshadows the director's later masterpieces, from Psycho to North by Northwest and from The Birds to Frenzy.\n\nRated PG · Released 18 Oct 2024 · France, United Kingdom · Language: English · 72 min\nStudio: StudioCanal UK, Nedland Films, Turner Classic Movies\n\nOn your server — Audio: English","releaseInfo":"2024","genres":["Documentary","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"6.4","runtime":"72 min","cast":["Elvis Mitchell","Alfred Hitchcock"],"director":["Laurent Bouzereau"],"released":"2024-10-18T00:00:00.000Z","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Laurent Bouzereau","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/1gVpS5EGGwXXry6xSXo8xfkDlBu.jpg"},{"name":"Elvis Mitchell","character":"Narrator","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/pvBT0ZqswYgjgwSMfwIizsa8KpP.jpg"},{"name":"Alfred Hitchcock","character":"Self (archive footage)","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/osE39XteDT85B6sML8uTXFFv1sb.jpg"}]},"trailers":[{"source":"_lFZ45Yx004","type":"Clip"}],"trailerStreams":[{"title":"Clip: Clip","ytId":"_lFZ45Yx004"}],"writer":["Laurent Bouzereau"],"country":"France, United Kingdom, United Sta